## Entry schema

Every lesson uses this structure. The ID is sequential (`L-0001`, `L-0002`, …).

```markdown
### L-NNNN — <short imperative title> (<category>)

- **Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
- **Trigger:** <what the user corrected / what went wrong — describe the pattern, not just the instance>
- **Root cause:** <why the mistake happened — missing context? wrong assumption? ignored rule? edge case?>
- **Rule:** <imperative rule to prevent recurrence — "Always …", "Never …", "Before doing X, check Y">
- **Applies to:** <files, patterns, or situations where this rule matters>
- **Status:** active
```

### Status values

| Status                          | Meaning                                                                                  |
| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `active`                        | This rule is in effect. The agent must respect it.                                       |
| `superseded by L-XXXX`          | A newer lesson refines or replaces this one. Read the newer one instead.                 |
| `graduated to <FILE>.md`        | This rule proved so fundamental it was promoted to a permanent rule file. Still readable. |

### Categories

Use exactly one of these tags per entry:

| Category        | When to use                                                     |
| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `coding`        | Code style, error handling, naming, imports, dead code.         |
| `design`        | UI, colours, typography, spacing, icons, motion, accessibility. |
| `database`      | Schema, migrations, queries, RLS, enums, types.                 |
| `deployment`    | Hosting, env vars, secrets, CI/CD, domains.                     |
| `security`      | Auth, PII, tokens, CORS, CSP, rate limiting.                    |
| `prompting`     | How to interpret user prompts, scope control, context loading.  |
| `architecture`  | Folder structure, module boundaries, dependency management.     |
| `performance`   | Bundle size, query speed, rendering, caching.                   |
| `documentation` | Doc updates missed, wrong file updated, stale pointers.         |
| `other`         | Anything that does not fit above.                                |

